body:
### Tested versions

4.5.1-stable

### System information

Windows 11 - Forward+ - Nvidia GeForce 3080 Ti

### Issue description

Jittering occurs when moving a Camera 3D in orthographic view via a simple movement script.

```gdscript
func _process(delta: float) -> void:
	var inputDirection = Input.get_vector("move_left", "move_right", "move_up", "move_down")

	var movementDirection = (basis.x * inputDirection.x + basis.z * inputDirection.y)
	movementDirection = movementDirection.normalized()
	position += movementDirection * movementSpeed * delta
```
Video demonstrating the issue: [https://youtu.be/8XzxNgQmbFY](url)

### Steps to reproduce

1. Create a 3D scene with any model to act as a view anchor;
2. Create a Node 3D that will act as the camera pivot;
3. Create a Node3D as a child of the pivot that will act as the pitch controller;
4. Create a Camera3D as a child of the pivot;
5. Attach the following script to the camera pivot Node3D:
```gdscript
extends Node3D

@onready var camera_pitch: Node3D = $CameraPitch

var cameraHeight: float = 400.0
var movementSpeed: float = 70.0
var yawTarget: float = deg_to_rad(45.0)
var pitchTarget: float = deg_to_rad(-30.0)

func _ready() -> void:
	position.y = cameraHeight
	rotation.y = yawTarget
	camera_pitch.rotation.x = pitchTarget

func _process(delta: float) -> void:
	var inputDirection = Input.get_vector("move_left", "move_right", "move_up", "move_down")

	var movementDirection = (basis.x * inputDirection.x + basis.z * inputDirection.y)
	movementDirection = movementDirection.normalized()
	position += movementDirection * movementSpeed * delta
```

